      "title_align": "left",
      "section": "Coverage across the genome",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "Two tracks over the same coverage collection. Scroll to zoom into a locus, drag to pan along the genome, brush the axis to publish the chromosome and the position range as ordinary dashboard filters. The lower track follows that region instead of showing the whole reference. Depth is drawn as bars because GenomeSpy has no line mark. Per-sample lanes, the gene annotation lane and the mark type live in the Settings gear.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
    },
